      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 John Wiley & Sons A/S. Published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "In the dermatological literature, the term 'contact urticaria syndrome' is often used with patients presenting no symptoms of contact urticaria, but symptoms of adjacent mucous membranes evolving to a systemic allergic reaction. Contact urticaria refers to a wheal and flare reaction following external contact with a causative substance. Its use should be restricted to skin: a skin reaction after direct skin contact."
      },
